data.content:
The root cause is that **Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi 10.0** upgraded from **Microsoft.OpenApi v1.x to v2.x**, which targets OpenAPI 3.1. Here are the breaking changes and fixes:

## 1. `OpenApiString` / `OpenApiAny` types removed

`IOpenApiAny` and concrete types like `OpenApiString` are gone. Use `System.Text.Json.Nodes.JsonNode` instead:

```csharp
// Before (.NET 9)
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any;
param.Schema.Example = new OpenApiString("1.0");

// After (.NET 10)
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
```

## 2. `schema.Nullable` removed

OpenAPI 3.1 uses a `type` array with `"null"` instead of a `nullable` keyword. The `Type` property is now a flags enum (`JsonSchemaType`):

```csharp
// Before (.NET 9)
property.Value.Nullable = false;

// After (.NET 10)
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;
property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null; // remove null from type set
```

To *add* nullability: `property.Value.Type |= JsonSchemaType.Null;`

## 3. `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` dictionary syntax changed

It's no longer a `Dictionary<OpenApiSecurityScheme, IList<string>>`. It now has a `Scheme` and `Scopes` property:

```csharp
// Before (.NET 9)
operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
{
    new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
};

// After (.NET 10)
operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
{
    new()
    {
        Scheme = oAuthScheme,
        Scopes = scopes // IList<string>
    }
};
```

## 4. `OpenApiReference` / `ReferenceType` changes

`ReferenceType` is now `ReferenceType.SecurityScheme` → `ReferenceType.SecurityScheme` (same name but verify the namespace is `Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.References`). In v2, you can also use the strongly-typed reference wrapper:

```csharp
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.References;

var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("oauth2");
```

## Full corrected code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models.References;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("oauth2");
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new() { Scheme = oAuthScheme, Scopes = scopes }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
                property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

**Summary of namespace changes:**
- ❌ `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` → ✅ `System.Text.Json.Nodes`
- ❌ `new OpenApiString(...)` → ✅ `JsonValue.Create(...)`
- ❌ `schema.Nullable` → ✅ `schema.Type` flags with `JsonSchemaType.Null`
- ❌ `new OpenApiReference { Type = ..., Id = ... }` → ✅ `new OpenApiSecuritySchemeReference("id")`
